  "dom_id": "step-q237018",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Let $a=5i-4j+3k$ and $b=-7i+xj+k.$ Given that the scalar projection of $a$ onto $b$ is zero, find the value of $x.$",
  "worked_solution": "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its scalar projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals zero only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na\u22a5b\\,\u27f9\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =5\\cdot (-7)+(-4)\\cdot x+3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-4x-32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ -4x-32 & =0 \\\\ 4x & =-32 \\\\ x & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
